OL,3,AEx-BBC presenter questions role of
OL,4,ARoyal Family in new documentary
OL,5,
OL,6,FVeteran broadcaster John Humphrys has
OL,7,Fsaid the people of the United Kingdom
OL,8,Fshould "be able to choose our leaders"
OL,9,Fas he releases a documentary exploring
OL,10,Fthe role of the Royal Family.
OL,12,FHumphrys, who for decades was one of
OL,13,Fthe most prominent faces on the BBC, is
OL,14,Fpresenting a new Channel 4 documentary
OL,15,Fcalled The Royals: Time to Go?
OL,17,FSpeaking to BBC Radio Wales Breakfast,
OL,18,Fthe Cardiff-born presenter said he
OL,19,F"admires" King Charles III in many
OL,20,Fways, but said it was a "matter of
OL,21,Fchoice".
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
